/-!
# The descent of the sheet of [Stacks Project, Tag 0DT9] to an étale stage

Let `F : G' ⟶ G` be a morphism of affine groupoid schemes with finite locally free source and
target maps, cartesian source, target and stabilizer squares and étale map on object schemes. The
first conclusion of [Stacks Project, Tag 0DT9] is that the induced map `C → C'` on rings of
invariant functions is étale, and the argument for it is a descent: over a strictly henselian base
the "Claim" of the source text is available
(`AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidScheme.exists_section_of_strictlyHenselian`, a section of `U' ⟶ U`
whose sheet is an invariant clopen containing the fibre over the chosen point), and the general
case is obtained by base changing to the strict henselization `C^{sh}_p` and descending the
resulting decomposition to a finite étale stage.

This file is that descent, in three parts.

**The Claim on a base change.** For a flat strictly henselian local extension `C₁` of `C` and a
point of `Spec (C' ⊗[C] C₁)` above the closed point of `Spec C₁`, the base-changed map on object
schemes `U'₁ ⟶ U₁` admits a section which is an open immersion with closed invariant range, and
that range contains a point of `U'₁` above the chosen point.

**The sheet as one idempotent and one equation.** A section of the base-changed map with invariant
range is the same datum as an `A`-algebra map `A' ⟶ A ⊗[C] C₁` together with an idempotent of
`A' ⊗[C] C₁` generating the kernel of the attached retraction on tensor products and satisfying the
single invariance equation `(s'^♯ ⊗ id) e = (t'^♯ ⊗ id) e`; the two passages are inverse to one
another. That form is what a filtered colimit can carry.

**The two descents.** For `Λ` an ind-étale extension of `C`, an `A`-algebra map `A' ⟶ A ⊗[C] Λ`
factors through `A ⊗[C] D` for a single étale stage `D` — `A'` is of finite presentation over `A`
because `f : U' ⟶ U` is étale — and an equation between two elements of `B' ⊗[C] D` which holds
over `Λ` holds at a possibly later étale stage.

**What is not here.** The last step of the first conclusion — assembling the stage datum into an
étale cover of `Spec C'` through the chosen point and concluding by the source-cover criterion
`AlgebraicGeometry.etale_of_forall_exists_etale_comp` — is carried out in the next file,
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Groupoids.FiniteFlatAffine.EtaleInvariantRingMapAssembly`, where the
tag is registered on `AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidScheme.etale_invariantRingMap` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidScheme.isPullback_mapObjects`. Everything that assembly needs is here or
imported: the point transport of
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_point_specMap_of_ringEquiv_square`, the comparison morphism of two base
changes of `AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidScheme.tensorBaseRingComparison`, the three descent lemmas
below, étaleness at the image of a point of a sheet
(`AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidScheme.etaleAt_specMap_invariantRingMap_section_point`) and the étale
cover built from étaleness at a point
(`AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidScheme.exists_etale_comp_of_etaleAt_of_square`).

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidScheme.exists_section_of_strictlyHenselian_of_bijective` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidScheme.exists_section_tensorBaseRing_of_strictlyHenselian`: **the
  section of the "Claim" on a base change**, with its sheet invariant and containing a point above
  the chosen point of `Spec C'₁`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidScheme.exists_isIdempotentElem_ker_tensorRetraction_of_section` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidScheme.exists_section_of_isIdempotentElem_ker_tensorRetraction`: **the
  two passages between such a section and the idempotent of `A' ⊗[C] C₁` cutting out its range.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidScheme.exists_isIdempotentElem_ker_tensorRetraction`: the kernel of
  the retraction attached to any `A`-algebra map `A' ⟶ A ⊗[C] C₁` is generated by an idempotent.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidScheme.exists_etale_stage_map`: **an `A`-algebra map into
  `A ⊗[C] Λ` factors through a single étale stage**, and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidScheme.exists_map_of_algHom` moves such a map along a map of
  extensions.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidScheme.etaleAt_specMap_invariantRingMap_section_point`: **the map on
  invariant rings is étale at the image of a point of the sheet of an invariant section.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidScheme.exists_etale_comp_of_etaleAt_of_square`: an étale cover through
  a point at which a morphism is étale, across a commuting square of étale morphisms.

## Implementation notes

The chosen point above the closed point is carried between the tensor product presentation
`C' ⊗[C] C₁` of the new base ring and the invariant ring of the base change by
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_point_specMap_of_ringEquiv_square`, along the square of Tag 03BK
(`AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidScheme.invariantRingMap_baseChangeHom_comp_ofBijective`); étaleness at
a point travels the same square in the opposite direction by
`AlgebraicGeometry.etaleAt_specMap_of_ringEquiv_square`.

The assembly must use the source-cover criterion and not
`AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidScheme.etaleAt_specMap_invariantRingMap_of_tensorBaseRing`, whose
hypothesis is local finite presentation of `Spec C' ⟶ Spec C` — part of the conclusion being
proved.

Every statement whose type mentions a coordinate ring of a base change is kept out of rewriting:
the tensor algebra is done by lemmas over abstract rings, the identifications of coordinate rings
by lemmas over abstract objects of `CommRingCat`, and the geometry of a sheet by a lemma over an
abstract morphism of groupoid schemes. A monolithic tactic proof over those terms exhausts the
heartbeat budget.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03BK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03BK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DT9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DT9)

## Tags

groupoid scheme, invariant ring, étale, strict henselization, ind-étale descent
-/

